WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:04.680
I'm gonna use
everything in my power

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.640
to make your life miserable
until you stop doing what you're doing.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.800
I've never seen this
happen before in Australia.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.880
- There has been ongoing conflict.
- They're a YouTube phenomenon.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.600
It was f*****g game over.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.280
This is the future
of Australian hip-hop right here.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.920
Growing up,
we've always had run-ins with police.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.560
They just look at us like criminals.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.560
Where we're trying
to divert kids from violence,

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.280
this group was using lyrics
of inciting the acts of violence.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.400
Bro, this video is lit as f**k.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.960
Guess growing up around it,
we got sucked into it.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.640
Violence becomes the means
for you to achieve a status.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.440
There's nothing unique
about art that talks about violence.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.160
But for some reason, when it comes to hip-hop,
we're having that debate all over again.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.440
And I think it's because
of who's telling that story.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.160
If you're constantly
being profiled by police,

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.200
and you feel insecure and unsafe
in your own community,

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.640
you're gonna get angry.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.440
The real controversial aspect of ONEFOUR
definitely became a double-edged sword.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.760
It's like this yin and yang.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.360
You have the street,
and then you have the music.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:15.480
We start to see the violence escalate
with these street gangs.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:18.320
Lekks, my little brother,
and Celly got locked up.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.880
P got four years.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.640
Lekks got four years, and Celly got ten.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.920
I thought like, "How are we gonna be able
to hold up the crew while they're gone?"

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.240
They were just starting
to turn their lives around.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.480
And then they're back in trouble
with the police again.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.800
One thing I want people to understand,

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.920
is how important it is to
find something you love

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.680
and then run with it.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.880
That's the one thing that helped us

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.600
get out of a lot of the bulls**t
we had to go through.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.920
We knew that the police were gonna try
to do whatever they could to disrupt.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.200
We had no idea, like, to
what lengths they would go to.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.880
The way that the police are
being used to target ONEFOUR

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.160
is something that has
never been seen in Australia.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:10.120
Where we have a problem,

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.960
we are lawfully harassing that group,
and we don't apologise for that.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.640
But is the New South Wales
police an adequate judge

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.360
of what is acceptable and what's not?

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:23.640
Hip-hop is the biggest genre in the world.
And yet, we wanna deplatform it and censor it.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:27.880
If the police are successful
in destroying a group,

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.440
it's a dark day for Australia
and freedom of expression.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.040
You know,
there's a lot more to lose if you lose,

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.440
so we can't lose.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:40.800
If that's your thing,

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.880
it's gonna keep you out of trouble,
keep you busy

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.840
so you're not on the streets,
I'm good with that.

